    "text": "Connection Establishment 4 In) gheansmts data in|full-duplex mode. | When two TCPs in two machines are connected, they are able to send segments to each other simultaneously. Ta Way Rania) Lop > The connection establishment in TCP 1s called three way handshaking. > Suppose client, wants to make a connection with the server, using TCP as the transport layer protocol. > The process starts with the server. The server program tells its TCP that it 1s ready to accept a connection. This 1s called a request for a passive open. > The client program issues a request for an active open. A client that wishes to connect to an open server tells its TCP that it needs to be connected to that particular server. > TCP can now start the three-way handshaking process .",
